=== AC5 GET /api/v1/customer/cart/list (customer@nears.com, module_id=2: 2 rows,
item 390 on an active flash sale + item 388 plain) ===
STATUS=200  TOTAL_QUERIES=73  CATEGORY_Q=1  FLASH_Q=1  ADDON_Q=0
CartController::cartListResponse() (Api/V1/CartController.php:83-104) DOES batch
Category/FlashSaleItem/AddOn via buildCartPrefetch() — confirmed (1/1/0) — but
`Cart::where(...)->get()` (line 87-90) carries NO eager-load at all (no
->with('item.store.storeConfig','item.module',...)), so $cart->item (accessed at
line 92's partition filter) and every downstream $item->store / $item->module /
$item->store->storeConfig access inside cart_product_data_formatting() each
lazy-load PER ROW — unlike product_data_formatting()'s multi_data branch, which
DOES call ->loadMissing([...]) once (Helpers.php:409). CartController has no
equivalent loadMissing call. Baseline (Jira): 138 queries / 8 rows (17.25/row).

=== AC6 GET /api/v1/customer/wish-list (customer@nears.com, 10 items in module 1,
5 on active flash sales: items 97/3/98/215/8) ===
STATUS=200  TOTAL_QUERIES=257  CATEGORY_Q=1  FLASH_Q=1  ADDON_Q=0
Baseline (Jira): 192 queries / 18 rows. wishlist_data_formatting's own
Category/FlashSaleItem/AddOn batching (buildWishlistItemPrefetch, Helpers.php
~1211-1240) is confirmed working (1/1/0), but each item still goes through
product_data_formatting(..., multi_data:false, ...) which independently computes
nutritions_name/allergies_name/generic_name/tax_data via lazy relation access +
4 more whereIn queries PER ITEM (Helpers.php ~510-523) — untouched by this diff.

=== Root cause (confirmed by direct code read, Helpers.php:401-536) ===
product_data_formatting()'s multi_data==true branch (the ticket's primary target)
DOES batch Category/FlashSaleItem/AddOn (lines 411-434) into O(1) queries, and DOES
loadMissing(['store.storeConfig','store.discount','store.translations',
'store.storage','unit','module']) once (line 409). But lines 510-523 (UNCHANGED by
this diff — outside the diff hunks) still run, per item inside the SAME foreach:
  $item?->nutritions            (lazy relation load)
  $item?->allergies             (lazy relation load)
  $item?->generic                (lazy relation load)
  $item?->pharmacy_item_details  (lazy relation load)
  $item?->ecommerce_item_details (lazy relation load, via ->brand_id/->is_basic/...)
  $item?->taxVats()->pluck(...)  (METHOD call — always re-queries, no
                                   relationLoaded() guard, same bug class NEARS-2986
                                   fixed elsewhere but not here)
  $item?->seoData                (lazy relation load, ecommerce module_type only)
  + 4 whereIn queries (Nutrition/Allergy/GenericName/Tax) when those relations are
    non-empty.
None of these 7 relations are in the loadMissing() list added by this diff. The
solution doc (docs/solutions/NEARS-2984-product-data-formatting-batch.md,
"Rejected alternative" section) states: "Verified the multi-branch computes zero
queries for these today (fields are absent from the listing response entirely,
not merely per-item)" — this is FALSIFIED by direct code read: the fields ARE
present in the multi_data branch's own foreach (lines 510-523, same file, same
function, just below the diff's own last hunk) and DO cost queries per item
whenever an item has any nutrition/allergy/generic/tax data. This is very likely
why the ~11-13 queries/item marginal cost persists across every list route
measured above.
